WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Kelly] Well I know

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.040
as I mentioned earlier

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.040
we have some of our most
memorable rad humans here

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.330
to share in this special event today

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.845
'cause I didn't wanna hog you for myself.

00:00:09.845 --> 00:00:10.678
- (laughs)

00:00:10.678 --> 00:00:12.450
- [Kelly] I'm Southern, I share.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.330
So they have some questions for Dr. Biden.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.350
Let's start with Dr.
Patrick a fellow educator.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.130
- Oh, okay.
- Like the First Lady.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.630
- He is the founder of

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.210
Man Up Teacher Fellowship.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.400
- Oh, I know Man Up.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.680
- Oh, you do? Oh awesome!

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.420
Well it's an organization
that we highlighted

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.470
that encourages more men of
color to become teachers.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.553
So Dr. Patrick, what would
you like to ask Dr. Biden?

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:35.645
- Call me Jill.

00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:41.509
- Hi Jill, hi Dr Biden.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.350
- It feels odd, I can't do it either.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.921
- [Dr. Patrick] I know yeah.

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:48.440
I thank you for being an advocate

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.890
for educators and for education.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.340
We are thrilled to have an educator

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.770
in the white house and I'm truly humbled

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.991
and certainly proud to
get to meet you today.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.824
- [Jill] Thank you.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:00:59.750
- [Dr. Patrick] My question for you is

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.450
as an educator and a parent

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.820
what is your message
to teachers and parents

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.950
struggling with the toll
the pandemic is taking

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:09.990
on their children.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.967
- [Jill] Yeah, it has
been so tough you know

00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:14.403
and I see it in my own classroom,

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:16.720
on zoom of course.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.930
But you know it's been
really hard for teachers

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.830
and parents and kids.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:25.200
And I think that we're all struggling and

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.230
I think when we get
back into the classroom,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:31.130
you know mental health is
going to be a big issue.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.180
We gotta help heal these kids

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.920
and you know yourself I mean,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.430
kids have been dealing
with food insecurity,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.180
domestic violence, child abuse

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.760
so many things that they're going to be

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.580
bringing back with them into the classroom

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.860
and teachers are gonna need help

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.670
and that's one of the
things I love about Joe.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.660
I love about those dinners at night.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.130
I can say to him, "Joe, we need this,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.840
you got to do this we're counting on you.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.580
The teachers are counting on you."

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.333
And so,

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.580
that's why I keep saying
we got to have hope

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.150
because things will be better.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.370
We're going to be back
in those classrooms.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.660
There's going to be broadband.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.810
I mean, I'm just so excited about,

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.590
you know the direction that
education is going to take

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.550
because we have to look at this
pandemic like an opportunity

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.760
to change the things
that didn't work, right?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.886
That's what we're going to do

00:02:21.886 --> 00:02:22.730
- Absolutely.
- [Jill] As teachers,

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.510
that's what we're going to do, yeah.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.343
- [Kelly] I think that you're right.

00:02:25.343 --> 00:02:26.970
See the mental health thing is going to be

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.660
like just with my four and six year old.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.240
Like it's incredible and
all the different ages

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.010
and it was so funny just
to add in a little bit,

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.963
my mother who's also a teacher.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.830
I'm actually a songwriter because of her.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.210
Like I had a problem with
mental illness when I was a kid

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.580
I just was very much an introvert.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.958
I know it's hard to believe.

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:46.798
(laughing)

00:02:46.798 --> 00:02:48.950
- It is.
- [Kelly] Unbelievable.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.100
But I was, and I had a I had a problem

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.110
because of our family life
and things and circumstances

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.260
getting my emotions out and so writing.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.273
So it's interesting that you.

00:02:57.273 --> 00:02:58.106
- Yes.

00:02:58.106 --> 00:02:58.939
Cathartic.
- [Kelly] You teach writing

00:02:58.939 --> 00:02:59.900
it's very cathartic

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.860
and so I started just writing
and getting things out

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.620
and it turned into poetry
and it turned into songs.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.090
And I think, I don't know

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:07.910
I truly do believe if we do this right,

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.560
so many beautiful artists are
going to come out of this.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.570
As far as like children,
especially in teenagers

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.750
because there's so many emotions going on

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.720
and there just needs to be that outlet.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:18.970
- [Jill] Yeah, exactly.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.000
And that's why I tell parents all the time

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.710
get your kids to write about this moment.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.500
They can, you know, do it over video.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.850
They can do it through artwork,
whatever medium they choose

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.440
but it will provide catharsis for them.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.380
And we shouldn't forget this moment.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.230
We shouldn't forget it.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.690
We should remember you know
what we learned about ourselves

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:44.630
and use this to reflect on
how we can make things better.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.640
- [Kelly] Yeah, we don't want to forget it

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.500
because we also don't
want to repeat it, people.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.770
- [Jill] Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.570
- God bless history.
- [Jill] Yeah.

